Revision history for Authen-WebAuthn
 
Unreleased
  - Decode client-supplied CBOR with CBOR::XS->new_safe, so that a tagged
    value cannot instantiate a Perl object
  - Fix PS256 signature verification (32 byte salt)
  - Fix trust_anchors given as a code reference, which was always refused
  - Support ES384, ES512 and EdDSA (Ed25519) credential keys, and
    Ed25519 attestation certificates
  - Add allowed_algs option to validate_registration
  - origin can be an arrayref of accepted origins (Frank Carnovale)
  - Refuse cross-origin requests unless allow_cross_origin is set
    (behaviour change)
  - Add appid option to validate_assertion, for AppIDs other than the
    origin
  - Add generate_registration_options and generate_assertion_options
  - Return user_verified, backup_eligible and backup_state
  - Reject a Backup State flag without Backup Eligibility
  - Reject credential IDs longer than 1023 bytes
  - At registration, reject a credential public key that does not parse,
    whose key type does not match its algorithm, or an RSA key under 2048
    bits
  - Malformed input is refused with a message of its own, without Perl
    warnings, and CBOR tags are refused
  - Authen::WebAuthn::Test produces RSA, P-384, P-521 and Ed25519 keys,
    and packed self attestation
  - A test PKI (t/pki) and certificate attestation in
    Authen::WebAuthn::Test, both packed and fido-u2f
  - Report a missing Basic Constraints extension in a packed attestation
    certificate, which failed with a Perl error
  - Tests reach every statement; the few that cannot be reached are
    marked uncoverable
  - Token Binding is no longer checked, as no browser supports it and
    WebAuthn Level 3 removed it; token_binding_id_b64 is ignored

0.005
  - Add allow_unknown_attestation_format option

0.004
  - Add allow_untrusted_attestation option

0.003 2023-11-09
  - Update Crypt::OpenSSL::X509::Extension and Net::SSLeay dependancies
  - Make sure Net::SSLeay is initialized before use

0.002 2023-11-09
  - Supported attestation types: none, packed, fido-u2f
  - Mandatory attestation trust chain validation

0.001 2022-01-21
  - initial release
  - Authentication and registration without attestation
  - ECC/RSA keys supported
